title three remotes take their names, and the two piers become one tree
prompt Keaton asked to rename the remotes -- xykj61 to xy, debrided to debrided, later grain-os to seed -- then to resolve the Mantra weave conflicts so the new tools/l/launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish could run, and to send once upstream reconciled.
think A rebase was the rota's word and the wrong tool here: all twelve local commits touch the same four living ledgers, so pull --rebase meant twelve rounds of one conflict against three upstream commits. One merge resolves it once, and the tree already carries the shape -- construction: merge two piers, reconcile %226.
think Eleven of the twenty-one conflicts were both piers repairing the SAME BSD-dialect red two ways. This pier had factored the repair into tools/fixtures/shell_portable.sh (xargs_lines, stamp_epoch, stamp_ahead, DP_REF_RE); upstream had inlined tr '\n' '\0' | xargs -0 at each site. Ours held because it subsumes theirs and adds the empty-list guard, and DP_REF_RE was checked character-for-character against the pattern upstream inlined rather than assumed equal.
think dated_path_exclusions.sh wanted a union rather than a side: this pier's pole debride plus upstream's mitra shed, twenty-four LISTED basenames, each of the three contested names checked absent from git ls-files and still referenced before it was written down.
think The crux was the ledger. Both clones had allocated %233-%237 for entirely different reds -- %230 and %252 arriving a third time, and the card's own standing answer was aborted rather than renumbered. Keaton ruled renumber, so upstream's five re-seated at %271-%275 with their four intra-row citations repointed, and the citations outside the ledger followed: the mitra block in dated_path_exclusions.sh and the index row for log 20260826-141312.
think Rows %231-%232 had been folded twice, once per pier, onto two shelves holding the same two rows. A duplicate reds the monotone spine, so the duplicate went; the shelves differ only in the season-to-chapter wording, so no row lost a word.
obs The merge carried four reds of its own, none of them anybody's mistake and all of them the shape of two trees meeting. The REDS headline span still recited 1 to 270. template-manifest.bron classified arbor twice -- personal from this pier, scrub from upstream -- and personal held, because scrubbing would have shipped arbor/ to the public seed before its contents were cleared file by file. seed/arbor stood as a stale projection from when scrub was the verdict. And skate_macos_choice_witness.rish arrived from upstream on no roster at all, carrying witness_reach one past its ceiling; the ceiling only falls, so the witness was seated rather than the ceiling raised.
obs The rename broke more than it looked like it would, and the breakage was invisible until measured. git remote rename moves refs/remotes/origin/* , so every guard reading refs/remotes/origin/main lost its base: one_clock_provenance_scan.sh, dated_guard_scan.sh, and one_clock_witness.rish duty 4. The first sweep also repointed upstream_shape_scan.sh and had to be reverted whole -- every origin in that file names a throwaway pen clone, where git clone itself chose the name.
obs Every loop recipe spelled git pull --rebase xykj61 main, so the dream launcher would have refused on its first line. launch-sound-fixed-chapter.rish already said the remote named xy, which is upstream having anticipated exactly this rename.
obs The provenance base is now debrided/main by pure rename, preserving what it measured. Whether it should read xy/main -- the anointed ordering remote, which debrided mirrors after -- is a real question this round declined to answer silently; a lagging base weighs more artifacts, which is conservative rather than unsafe.
